ny tablets  as they could but that's just the 12  point 2 inch but really these are Pro  Series tablets so Samsung is antha  sizing the multitasking features in fact  these larger ones actually allow for 4  way multitasking mode that lets you drag  an app to each corner of the display  and use them all at the same time same  way as you could on the note 3 except  now you have four and that's actually  really useful with all these screen real  estate so this Plus Samsung's floating  window means you actually can probably  get some serious work done with multiple  applications open at the same time or so  at least they claim and this is all in  the new TouchWiz on top of Android 4.4  KitKat on all these tablets and you can  kind of tell by the great color scheme  and the notification bar and by some  other subtle changes but really it's all  about TouchWiz again and you could  probably never tell what version of  Android it's running if you didn't check  but the notification bar is the biggest  change I noticed it's way more colorful  and bold which is pretty amazing  considering how colorful and bold  TouchWiz was in the first place and  there's also a new whole tablet UI with  all these panels that reminds me a lot  of chameleon which was a launcher on  Android earlier that allowed you to move  around and resize the different panes  this basically does the same thing on a  sort of a TouchWiz colorful level but  other than that the new hardware was  pretty much what we'd expected out of  Samsung there were unfortunately no  front-facing speakers to be found on any  of these tablets but something really  really nice is that they all have 2560  by 1600 displays including the 8.4 inch  tab pro which i think makes it the  highest pixel density in any midsize  tablet form factor the rest of them are  up to 1080p so that's really nice and it  also has an 80 200 million power battery  to power it all and it's not really all  that thick as a high-end processor two  gigs of ram sounds like a really nice  device and of course I need to get my  hands on it and test it for myself to  know but if it's actually as good as it  seems I'm pretty excited for the Tab pro  8.4 oh and also these pro series tablets  all have sim cards so you could  technically make phone calls from them  if you're into that but either way  that's minute guys I was actually really  excited to see these new tablets the pro  series even though the note and Tab  series aren't going anywhere because  these are the first devices running  Android 4.4 KitKat and that have  TouchWiz on top of them so we'll likely  see a lot of these new improvements  maybe not the multitasking but a lot of  the enhancements in something like the  galaxy s5 when it comes out this year  with Android 4.4 KitKat on that so  that's our little sneak peek at the new  TouchWiz on phones but either way that's  been it so let me know what you guys  think of them thanks for watching  talk to you guys in the next one peace  [Music]
 

